                        "review": "[h1]Monumentally Mediocre[/h1]\n\nHonestly don't bother. Even with it's $2.59 price tag that's worth at least an hour's worth of gameplay it's absolutely not worth it. You can play Free Shooters that are a hell of a lot better than this, not to mention you could pay a couple dollars extra for something like Chop Goblins which is just as short as this but plays a million times better. When you're playing an FPS Game like a Cover Shooter, you know you screwed up and need to go back to base one.\n\nMost of the enemies either run towards you like a dumbass or spam projectiles to an absurd degree. Worse yet, you mainly fight them in cramped corridors that feel like you're going to be crushed by the walls. No horizontal angle in any of the corridors means you'll take unavoidable damage and even on Easy the beginning levels will have you dying constantly. The game at Level 3 becomes a mediocre shooter and the game sometimes opens up, but there's no complexity, no substance and the movement is just not very fun even when bunny hopping. Levels also have tons of backtracking and are a slog to get through.\n\nI do like the idea of the Teleport Gun though and honestly, they should have just focused the entire game on that alone. It could have been a cool Puzzle Game if they did that, but instead they opted to make the most worthless shooter possible. I've seen something on my Steam library for this game that the levels were actually hand drawn which is good, but these needed a lot more work. It's also buggy. Enemies get stuck on things and the music doesn't know when to loop. The music itself is mainly hard rock that is a bit better than most of the generic metal that a lot of shooters have these days, but the end screen song is actually awesome and now I have to find out what that song is because I was jamming with it for a couple minutes at the end.\n\nThere's just too much jank in order for this to be any good. At the very least it's not a lot but you would better spend your money on a much better game that's on sale for that price.",
